/-! # Fixed-degree divisors supported in a smooth open curve

Source: Stacks Project, moduli.tex, Tags 0DPE and 0DPI; pic.tex, Tags 0B9A,
0B9B, 0B9D and 0B9J (blueprint: lem-sfb-projective-smooth-divisor-parameter).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The degree-d Hilbert functor of the smooth open is represented by a finite-type open
of the projective constant-polynomial Hilbert scheme. The universal ideal on `C_V` restricts
to the universal Hilbert ideal on `U_V`, and its support lies in that open. Pulling back the
representing equivalence to every base, including a non-Noetherian one, gives the same
classifying maps. Pullback of the universal ideal gives relative divisors and their dual
ideal line bundles on every test scheme.

Source: Stacks Project, moduli.tex, Tags 0DPE and 0DPI; pic.tex, Tags 0B9A, 0B9B,
0B9D and 0B9J (blueprint: lem-sfb-projective-smooth-divisor-parameter).

Proof:
1. Apply lem-sfb-projective-hilbert-polynomial-representability to the specified embedding.
   For the constant polynomial d its universal family is finite locally free of degree d
   by lem-sfb-constant-hilbert-finite-locally-free. Closed immersions survive base change
   and composition (lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-base-change and -products).
2. Remove from H the closed image of the part of the universal family outside U.
   Finite morphisms are closed (lem-weil-pbc-finite-closed-map-finite-fibres). A boundary
   point survives every field extension by lem-weil-pbc-surjective-base-change, so a
   test map factors through this open exactly when its family is supported in U.
3. A finite locally free closed family in U_T is proper over T; C_T is separated, hence
   the immersion into C_T is proper and closed (lemma-nagata-proper-to-separated-target
   and lem-weil-pbc-proper-immersion-closed). Its fibre polynomial is d by the numerical
   bridge. Thus its unique Hilbert classifying map factors through V. Conversely pullback
   gives the original ideal, naturally, by lem-pc-hilb-functorial. The pushforward rank
   convention agrees by lem-pc-flf-properties and lem-weil-pbc-finite-free-algebra-spectrum.
4. H is Noetherian by lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian, so its open V is of finite
   presentation (lem-sfb-noetherian-open-closed-finite-presentation). Composition is finite
   type by lem-sfb-finite-type-composition-base-change.
5. On U_V the universal ideal is Cartier by lem-pc-cartier-criterion and smooth base
   change (lem-sbc-smooth-relative-dimension-permanence). Off its support the ideal is
   generated by 1. These opens cover C_V, so it is Cartier there and flat over V, hence
   relative effective Cartier. Its dual ideal module is the divisor line bundle.
6. Fibre-product identities and ideal pullback give representation after arbitrary base
   change, with no Noetherian assumption on the new base. Finite presentation survives
   base change (lem-weil-pbc-qcqs-morphism-permanence). The flat ideal sequence stays exact
   by lem-sfb-flat-closed-family-ideal-base-change. Locally a generator and its dual pull
   back to a generator and its dual; their inverse-unit transition functions agree,
   giving the asserted pullback isomorphism of divisor lines.
-/
theorem exists_projective_smooth_divisor_parameter
    (S : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian S] [CompactSpace S]
    (C : Over S) (n : ℕ) (i : C.left ⟶ ℙ(ULift.{u} (Fin (n + 1)); S))
    [IsClosedImmersion i] (hi : i ≫ (ℙ(ULift.{u} (Fin (n + 1)); S) ↘ S) = C.hom)
    [Flat C.hom] [LocallyOfFinitePresentation C.hom]
    [QuasiCompact C.hom] [QuasiSeparated C.hom]
    (hpure : ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] (s : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ S),
      (pullback C.hom s).IsPureDimension 1)
    (U : C.left.Opens) [SmoothOfRelativeDimension 1 (U.ι ≫ C.hom)] (d : ℕ) :
    ∃ (H : Over S) (JH : (pullback C.hom H.hom).IdealSheafData)
      (V : Over S) (e : (hilbertPresheaf (U.ι ≫ C.hom) d).RepresentableBy V)
      (v : V ⟶ H) (J : (pullback C.hom V.hom).IdealSheafData)
      (j : pullback (U.ι ≫ C.hom) V.hom ⟶ pullback C.hom V.hom),
      IsHProjective H.hom ∧
      IsProperHilbertFamily C.hom H JH ∧
      HasProjectiveFibreHilbertPolynomial C.hom i H JH (Polynomial.C (d : ℚ)) ∧
      (∀ (T : Over S) (I : (pullback C.hom T.hom).IdealSheafData),
        (IsProperHilbertFamily C.hom T I ∧
          HasProjectiveFibreHilbertPolynomial C.hom i T I (Polynomial.C (d : ℚ))) ↔
          ∃! k : T ⟶ H, I = JH.comap (baseChangeMap C.hom k)) ∧
      LocallyOfFiniteType V.hom ∧ QuasiCompact V.hom ∧ IsOpenImmersion v.left ∧
      j ≫ pullback.fst C.hom V.hom = pullback.fst (U.ι ≫ C.hom) V.hom ≫ U.ι ∧
      j ≫ pullback.snd C.hom V.hom = pullback.snd (U.ι ≫ C.hom) V.hom ∧
      J = JH.comap (baseChangeMap C.hom v) ∧
      IsClosedImmersion ((e.homEquiv (𝟙 V)).1.subschemeι ≫ j) ∧
      J = ((e.homEquiv (𝟙 V)).1.subschemeι ≫ j).ker ∧
      J.comap j = (e.homEquiv (𝟙 V)).1 ∧
      J.IsRelativeEffectiveCartier (pullback.snd C.hom V.hom) ∧
      J.toModulesᵛ.IsInvertible ∧
      (∀ (T : Over S) (k : T ⟶ V),
        (e.homEquiv k).1 = (e.homEquiv (𝟙 V)).1.comap
          (baseChangeMap (U.ι ≫ C.hom) k) ∧
        (J.comap (baseChangeMap C.hom k)).IsRelativeEffectiveCartier
          (pullback.snd C.hom T.hom) ∧
        Nonempty ((J.comap (baseChangeMap C.hom k)).toModulesᵛ ≅
          (Scheme.Modules.pullback (baseChangeMap C.hom k)).obj J.toModulesᵛ)) ∧
      (∀ (B : Scheme.{u}) (g : B ⟶ S),
        ∃ (VB : Over B) (b : (Over.map g).obj VB ⟶ V)
          (eB : ((Over.map g).op ⋙ hilbertPresheaf (U.ι ≫ C.hom) d).RepresentableBy VB),
          IsPullback b.left VB.hom V.hom g ∧
          ∀ (T : Over B) (k : T ⟶ VB),
            eB.homEquiv k = e.homEquiv ((Over.map g).map k ≫ b)) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
